# This file has never run against this tree. The workspace is not a git
# repository, so nothing here has been exercised by a real `git status`.
#
# It has been exercised somewhere else: every rule below, and every negation,
# was checked with `git check-ignore` in a throwaway repository holding a
# skeleton of this tree — that the `mawarid` README survives the wildcard above
# it, that `vendor/retour/Cargo.toml.orig` survives `*.orig`, that `app.png`
# survives `/*.png`, that `.env.example` survives `.env.*`. That test proves the
# patterns mean what they say. It does not prove they cover everything this
# repository will actually produce.
#
# So: treat the first `git add -A` as the real test, and read what it staged
# before you commit it.

# Rust
/target/
# The old-baseline container build's collected artifacts
# (apps/studio/src-tauri/linux/ibni.sh); the staging copy and its own
# target directory live under ~/.cache/taarib-bina-linux, outside the tree.
/dist-linux/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb
# `llvm-tools` is a declared toolchain component, and a coverage run drops
# these beside the binary rather than inside the target directory.
*.profraw
*.profdata
# `/target/` is anchored because a cargo workspace has one target directory at
# its root. Two cases sit outside it: `vendor/retour` is excluded from the
# workspace, so building it on its own produces a target directory nothing
# above catches, and the Tauri crate is sometimes built from its own directory.
vendor/*/target/

# Node / frontend
node_modules/
apps/studio/dist/
apps/studio/.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo
.pnpm-store/
npm-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# Tauri
apps/studio/src-tauri/target/
apps/studio/src-tauri/gen/

# C# / Unity plugins
unity/**/bin/
unity/**/obj/
unity/**/*.user
unity/.vs/

# Script adapter builds
adapters-script/*/dist/
adapters-script/*/node_modules/

# WebAssembly build output
crates/taarib-wasm/pkg/

# Packaging output
packaging/out/
*.AppImage
*.snap

# Local machine state that must never be committed: signing keys, user data,
# registry caches, downloaded patches, extracted game strings.
#
# The key extensions are a wider net than anything this repository is expected
# to produce. Custody of every private key is the OS keychain, so a file with
# one of these names is by definition a mistake, and the cost of catching a
# mistake that has not happened yet is one line each.
*.key
*.pem
*.der
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p8
*.pk8
*.ppk
id_rsa
id_ed25519
id_ecdsa
mafatih/
sandooq/
makhbaa/
nusakh/
sijillat/
*.ruqaa
taarib.db
taarib.db-wal
taarib.db-shm
idadat.local.json

# Taarib reads no `.env` file and no code here loads one. The rule exists so
# that a habit picked up from another project cannot quietly deposit provider
# credentials in a repository that has never held any.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Fonts are vendored per assets/fonts/README.md; their archives are not, and
# neither are the font binaries themselves: `assets/fonts/` holds the manifest
# and the README, and packaging fetches the faces into `naskh/`, `kufi/`,
# `sans/` and `latin/` at the versions `khutut.json` pins. The interface's own
# eight Plex faces under `apps/studio/src/khutut/` are a separate, deliberately
# committed copy and are not covered by this rule — see assets/NOTICES.md.
#
# Honest note: these six lines guard a directory nothing fills. `assets/fonts/`
# holds `khutut.json` and `README.md` and has never held a face; the fetched
# faces land in `apps/studio/src-tauri/mawarid/khutut/`, which the `mawarid/*`
# rule at the foot of this file already excludes. Keeping them costs nothing
# and catches the plausible mistake of downloading a face by hand into the
# directory the manifest is in — but they are not, and never were, what stops
# font binaries reaching the repository.
assets/fonts/**/*.zip
assets/fonts/**/*.tar.gz
assets/fonts/**/*.ttf
assets/fonts/**/*.otf
assets/fonts/**/*.woff
assets/fonts/**/*.woff2

# Python tooling in scripts/ is run in place; its bytecode cache is not source.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Screenshots taken while developing land in the repository root by default,
# and three had accumulated here: two unreferenced, and one that carried a
# developer's home directory — `C:\Users\<name>\AppData\Roaming\Taarib` — into
# the tree as rendered pixels, where no text search would ever have found it.
# Project artwork lives in assets/huwiya/ and apps/studio/src-tauri/ayqunat/.
#
# `app.png` is excepted because README.md embeds it. Before committing a
# replacement, read the image: the footer status strip prints the data root,
# so capture it under a profile whose name is not yours, or redact that strip.
/*.png
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg
/*.gif
/*.webp
/*.mp4
!/app.png

# Merge and patch droppings. `vendor/retour/Cargo.toml.orig` is a genuine
# committed file — `cargo vendor` writes it, and it is what the patch described
# in vendor/retour/TAARIB.md can be diffed against. The negation exists so that
# catching a merge-conflict `.orig` does not silently drop the provenance of
# the one vendored crate in the tree.
*.orig
!vendor/**/Cargo.toml.orig
*.rej

# Editors
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
*.code-workspace
.zed/
.fleet/
.helix/
.nvim.lua
*.swp
*.swo
*~

